# blink Rust rules

Enforced by `[workspace.lints]` and `just lint`. Never weaken the lints,
`clippy.toml`, or `rust-toolchain.toml` to make code pass.

- No `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic!`/`todo!`/`unimplemented!` outside tests.
  `thiserror` in libraries, `anyhow` only in `blink-app`.
- `unsafe` only in `blink-capture`, `blink-audio`, `blink-encode`. Each block
  gets a `// SAFETY:` comment and holds one unsafe operation; split otherwise.
- `#[expect(lint, reason = "...")]`, never `#[allow]`.
- Log with `tracing` only; no `println!`/`eprintln!`/`dbg!`.
- No `as` casts (use `From`/`TryFrom`); no panicking indexing in `blink-ring`
  and `blink-mux`.
- Windows code behind `#[cfg(windows)]`, deps under
  `[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]`.
- Document every public item.
- Hot path (see `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`): zero-copy GPU path, no CPU readback,
  no CUDA-core NVENC features, no per-frame allocation, capture/encode threads
  never block on I/O.
- Run `just check` before finishing.
